# Smart Kirana POS, Inventory & Khata System — Roo Code Project Rules

## 1. Store & Project Identity
- **Store Name**: Laxmi Vatsalya General Store (Owner: Pandurang Paradkar, Phone: `9404380326`)
- **Primary Shop ID**: `current_shop`
- **Primary Business Type**: `KIRANA_RETAIL`
- **Tech Stack**: React 18, TypeScript, Vite, Tailwind CSS, Dexie.js (IndexedDB offline-first), Supabase (PostgreSQL + Realtime WebSockets), Vitest.
- **Production URL**: `https://smart-kirana-drab.vercel.app`

## 2. Database & Cloud Sync Architecture
- **Local IndexedDB (`src/db/db.ts`)**: Offline-first primary store (`kiranaDb` / `db`).
- **Live Supabase Cloud (`src/services/cloudSyncService.ts`)**:
  - **Supabase URL**: `https://oyolyrptcfbudnwlxyyq.supabase.co`
  - **11 Connected Cloud Tables**:
    1. `shop_profile`
    2. `store_users`
    3. `wholesalers`
    4. `products`
    5. `customers` (includes `0000-WALK-IN` for walk-in POS bills)
    6. `sales_invoices`
    7. `sale_items`
    8. `khata_transactions`
    9. `inventory_logs`
    10. `daily_galla_sessions`
    11. `expenses_and_drawings`
  - **Rule**: Always sanitize payloads via `sanitizeTablePayloadForSupabase()` in `src/services/cloudSyncService.ts` before upserting to Supabase so local-only fields (`business_type`, `loan_account_id`, `is_loan_funded`, `sale_rate_type`, `approval_status`) never cause `42703` / `PGRST204` errors.

## 3. Core Accounting & POS Invariants
- **Integer Paisa Math (`src/utils/math.ts`)**: Always use `toPaise()`, `toRupees()`, `roundCurrency()`, and `roundQty()` to prevent floating-point drift.
- **Checkout Equation (`src/services/billingService.ts`)**:
  `subtotal_amount - discount_roundoff = grand_total = amount_paid_now + udhari_added`
- **Backdated Billing Support**: `CartTab.billDate` (`YYYY-MM-DD`) in `src/components/pos/POSView.tsx` passes `billDate` into `BillingService.executeCheckout()` and stamps `sales_invoices`, `khata_transactions`, `inventory_logs`, and `daily_galla_sessions` with the selected historical date.

## 4. Development, Test & Deployment Commands
- **Start Dev Server**: `npm run dev`
- **Run Unit Tests**: `npx vitest run`
- **Production Build**: `npm run build`
- **Deploy to Vercel Production**: `npx vercel --prod --yes`

